maining distance.\n\n4. **Conclusion**:\n   - The distance run by the fourth guard is \\(1000 - 850 = 150\\) meters.\n\nThus, the fourth guard ran \\(\\boxed{150}\\) meters to reach the intruder.", "ground_truth_solution": "1. First, calculate the perimeter of the rectangular object. The dimensions are \\(200 \\, \\text{meters} \\times 300 \\, \\text{meters}\\).\n   \n   Using the formula for the perimeter of a rectangle \\( P = 2(l + w) \\), where \\( l \\) is the length and \\( w \\) is the width, we have:\n\n   \\[\n   P = 2(200 + 300) = 2 \\times 500 = 1000 \\, \\text{meters}\n   \\]\n\n2. Note that wherever the intruder is located around the object, two guards positioned at diagonally opposite corners will run a total distance equivalent to the semi-perimeter of the rectangle. This can be rationalized by considering that each guard runs along the perimeter to the intruder, and the shortest path along the perimeter from one corner to another is effectively half the perimeter.\n\n3. Since three guards in total have run a combined distance of \\( 850 \\, \\text{meters} \\), calculate the total distance all four guards would cover if running a combined distance equivalent to the perimeter:\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total distance} = P = 1000 \\, \\text{meters}\n   \\]\n\n4. Determine the distance the fourth guard must have run by subtracting the total distance the three guards have covered from the total perimeter:\n\n   \\[\n   \\text{Distance run by the fourth guard} = 1000 \\, \\text{meters} - 850 \\, \\text{meters} = 150 \\, \\text{meters}\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{150}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "In the decimal representation of a natural number \\( N \\), a 0 was inserted between the second and third digits from the right, resulting in \\( 9N \\). What could be the possible values of \\( N \\)? (List all possible values).", "deepseek_reasoning": "Okay, let's try to figure 