nd simplifying the function \\( f(x) \\):\n\n   \\[\n   f(x) = \\frac{1008 x^2 + 1009 + 2 \\sqrt{1008} \\sqrt{1009} x + \\sin(2018x)}{2016 x^2 + 2018}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Separate constant and variable parts**:\n\n   Break the fraction into two separate parts:\n   \n   \\[\n   f(x) = \\frac{1008 x^2 + 1009}{2016 x^2 + 2018} + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{1008} \\sqrt{1009} x + \\sin(2018x)}{2016 x^2 + 2018}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Simplify the first part**:\n   \n   Notice that \\( \\frac{1008 x^2 + 1009}{2016 x^2 + 2018} \\) can be simplified:\n   \n   \\[\n   \\frac{1008 x^2 + 1009}{2016 x^2 + 2018} = \\frac{1}{2} \\frac{2(1008 x^2 + 1009)}{2(1008 x^2 + 1009)} = \\frac{1}{2}\n   \\]\n\n   Therefore, we can rewrite \\( f(x) \\) as follows:\n   \n   \\[\n   f(x) = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{2 \\sqrt{1008} \\sqrt{1009} x + \\sin(2018x)}{2016 x^2 + 1009}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Analyze the second part**:\n   \n   Define the remaining part as \\( g(x) \\):\n   \n   \\[\n   g(x) = \\frac{2 \\sqrt{1008} \\sqrt{1009} x + \\sin(2018x)}{2016 x^2 + 1009}\n   \\]\n   \n   Observe that \\( g(x) \\) is an odd function because both \\( x \\) and \\(\\sin(2018x)\\) are odd, and the denominator is even. This implies that \\( g(-x) = -g(x) \\).\n\n5. **Determine Maximum and Minimum values**:\n   \n   Since \\( g(x) \\) is an odd function, its maximum and minimum values of \\( g \\) at \\( x \\) will be equal in magnitude but opposite in sign. The overall function \\( f(x) \\) thus will have:\n   \n   \\[\n   M = \\frac{1}{2} + \\max(g(x))\n   \\]\n   \n   \\[\n   m = \\frac{1}{2} + \\min(g(x)) = \\frac{1}{2} - \\max(g(x))\n   \\]\n   \n   Hence, their sums add up to:\n\n   \\[\n   M + m = \\left(\\frac{1}{2} + \\max(g(x))\\right) + \\left(\\frac{1}{2} - \\max(g(x))\\right) = \\frac{1}{2} + \\frac{1}{2} = 1\n   \\]\n\n### Conclusion:\n\\[\n\\boxed{1}\n\\]", "domain": "math", "source": "numina_math", "test_cases": null, "starter_code": null}, {"problem": "Let \\( A_1 \\), \\( B_1 \\), and \\( C_1 \\) be the points where 