 (2): b\u00b2 = (H\u00b2 s\u00b2 ) / [4 (s\u00b2 + 12 H\u00b2 ) ]\n\nLet me denote k = H/s, so H = k s. Then, substituting into equations:\n\nEquation (1): a\u00b2 = ( (k s )\u00b2 s\u00b2 ) / [4 (s\u00b2 + 3 (k s )\u00b2 ) ] = (k\u00b2 s^4 ) / [4 s\u00b2 (1 + 3 k\u00b2 ) ] = (k\u00b2 s\u00b2 ) / [4 (1 + 3 k\u00b2 ) ]\n\nSimilarly, equation (2): b\u00b2 = ( (k s )\u00b2 s\u00b2 ) / [4 (s\u00b2 + 12 (k s )\u00b2 ) ] = (k\u00b2 s^4 ) / [4 s\u00b2 (1 + 12 k\u00b2 ) ] = (k\u00b2 s\u00b2 ) / [4 (1 + 12 k\u00b2 ) ]\n\nSo from both equations, we can express a\u00b2 and b\u00b2 in terms of k and s. But note that both a\u00b2 and b\u00b2 are proportional to (k\u00b2 s\u00b2 ). Let me write:\n\nFrom equation (1):\n\na\u00b2 = (k\u00b2 s\u00b2 ) / [4 (1 + 3 k\u00b2 ) ] => 4 a\u00b2 (1 + 3 k\u00b2 ) = k\u00b2 s\u00b2 --- (1a)\n\nFrom equation (2):\n\nb\u00b2 = (k\u00b2 s\u00b2 ) / [4 (1 + 12 k\u00b2 ) ] => 4 b\u00b2 (1 + 12 k\u00b2 ) = k\u00b2 s\u00b2 --- (2a)\n\nSince both equal k\u00b2 s\u00b2, set them equal to each other:\n\n4 a\u00b2 (1 + 3 k\u00b2 ) = 4 b\u00b2 (1 + 12 k\u00b2 )\n\nDivide both sides by 4:\n\na\u00b2 (1 + 3 k\u00b2 ) = b\u00b2 (1 + 12 k\u00b2 )\n\nBring all terms to left side:\n\na\u00b2 + 3 a\u00b2 k\u00b2 - b\u00b2 - 12 b\u00b2 k\u00b2 = 0\n\nFactor terms:\n\n(a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 ) + k\u00b2 (3 a\u00b2 - 12 b\u00b2 ) = 0\n\nLet me factor out 3 from the second term:\n\n(a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 ) + 3 k\u00b2 (a\u00b2 - 4 b\u00b2 ) = 0\n\nSo:\n\n(a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 ) + 3 k\u00b2 (a\u00b2 - 4 b\u00b2 ) = 0\n\nLet me solve for k\u00b2:\n\n3 k\u00b2 (a\u00b2 - 4 b\u00b2 ) = -(a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 )\n\nThus,\n\nk\u00b2 = -(a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 ) / [3 (a\u00b2 - 4 b\u00b2 ) ] = (b\u00b2 - a\u00b2 ) / [3 (a\u00b2 - 4 b\u00b2 ) ]\n\nSimplify numerator and denominator:\n\nk\u00b2 = (b\u00b2 - a\u00b2 ) / [3 (a\u00b2 - 4 b\u00b2 ) ] = -(a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 ) / [3 (a\u00b2 - 4 b\u00b2 ) ]\n\n= (a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 ) / [3 (4 b\u00b2 - a\u00b2 ) ]\n\nSo,\n\nk\u00b2 = (a\u00b2 - b\u00b2 )