ation given:\n   \\[\n   |5x + y| + |5x - y| = 20\n   \\]\n\n2. First, square both sides of the given equation:\n   \\[\n   (|5x + y| + |5x - y|)^2 = 20^2\n   \\]\n\n3. Simplify the equation:\n   \\[\n   (|5x + y| + |5x - y|)^2 = 400\n   \\]\n\n4. Apply the binomial expansion on the left side:\n   \\[\n   |5x + y|^2 + 2|5x + y||5x - y| + |5x - y|^2 = 400\n   \\]\n\n5. Recognize that:\n   \\[\n   (5x + y)^2 = 25x^2 + y^2 + 2(5x)(y) = 25x^2 + y^2 + 10xy\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   (5x - y)^2 = 25x^2 + y^2 - 2(5x)(y) = 25x^2 + y^2 - 10xy\n   \\]\n\n6. Therefore:\n   \\[\n   |5x + y|^2 + |5x - y|^2 = (25x^2 + y^2 + 10xy) + (25x^2 + y^2 - 10xy) = 50x^2 + 2y^2\n   \\]\n\n7. Replace this back into the squared equation:\n   \\[\n   2(25x^2 + y^2) + 2|25x^2 - y^2| = 400\n   \\]\n\n8. Divide through by 2:\n   \\[\n   25x^2 + y^2 + |25x^2 - y^2| = 200\n   \\]\n\n9. Now solve the cases based on the absolute value expression $|25x^2 - y^2|$:\n\n   **Case 1**: \\(25x^2 \\ge y^2\\):\n   \\[\n   25x^2 + y^2 + (25x^2 - y^2) = 200\n   \\]\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   50x^2 = 200 \\implies x^2 = \\frac{200}{50} = 4 \\implies x = \\pm 2\n   \\]\n   Since \\(25x^2 \\ge y^2\\):\n   \\[\n   4 \\cdot 25 \\ge y^2 \\implies 100 \\ge y^2 \\implies |y| \\le 10\n   \\]\n\n   **Case 2**: \\(25x^2 \\le y^2\\):\n   \\[\n   25x^2 + y^2 + (y^2 - 25x^2) = 200\n   \\]\n   Simplifying:\n   \\[\n   2y^2 = 200 \\implies y^2 = 100 \\implies y = \\pm 10\n   \\]\n   Since \\(25x^2 \\le y^2\\):\n   \\[\n   25x^2 \\le 100 \\implies x^2 \\le 4 \\implies |x| \\le 2\n   \\]\n\n10. With these values of \\(x\\) and \\(y\\), the possible points \\(P(x, y)\\) on the plane are:\n    \\[\n    A(2, -10), B(2, 10), C(-2, 10), D(-2, -10)\n    \\]\n\n11. Next, evaluate \\(Q = x^2 - xy + y^2\\):\n\n    - On the edge \\(AB\\), evaluate \\(x = 2\\) and \\(|y| \\le 10\\):\n      \\[\n      Q = 4 - 2y + y^2\n      \\]\n      Find critical points by considering end values \\(y = -10\\) and \\(y = 10\\):\n      \\[\n      Q = 4 + 20 + 1